&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;br&gt;Visit druva.com and follow us on LinkedIn, X and Facebook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is seeking to hire a Sales Engineer with a focus on Data Protection with AI &amp;amp;amp;Data Security. As a Sales Engineer, you will provide technical direction and business guidance to the regional sales teams. We are looking for a motivated and proactive&lt;br&gt;individual to help exceed sales targets by driving innovative technical programs, conducting customer demonstrations, POCs, and overseeing daily technical solutioning activities. You will be responsible for evangelizing, positioning, and&lt;br&gt;architecting Druva’s Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security Solutions to a mix of new &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrates technical leadership and subject matter expertise on fully managed cloud-native SaaS, Endpoint &amp;amp;amp; Server Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security, and Cyber Resiliency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Provides technical leadership and direction to customers and internal staff in the development of Druva solutions, supporting pre-sales activities within the assigned region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Leverage technical discovery and qualification fundamentals to establish rapport as a trusted advisor to develop and propose solutions that meet the technology and business requirements of prospective &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Meet business objectives by collaborating with Sales Executives in the region&lt;br&gt;• Assist in delivering technical enablement to the Druva Channel Partner ecosystem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp;5 &amp;nbsp;to 8 years in technical customer-facing roles with at least 2+ years as a sales engineer working with enterprise software solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of enterprise server backup technologies&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Virtualization Platforms VMWare, HyperV, Nutanix &amp;amp;amp; ProxMox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Databases such as MS-SQL, Oracle, Azure SQL.&lt;br&gt;• Working knowledge &amp;amp;amp; understanding of AI concepts and tools. Hands on knowledge of Claude, Copilot would be added advantage.&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level knowledge of operating systems, including MS Windows, Linux,&amp;amp; amp; macOS.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with Active Directory, Entra ID, SSO, MFA, SCCM, and automated deployment tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of industry AI.&lt;br&gt;• Basic understanding of network technologies and protocols – TCP/IP, VLAN, DNS, switches, firewalls, routers, and proxies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Entrepreneurial - willing to go the extra mile, strong work ethic, resourceful, “get it&lt;br&gt;done” attitude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A highly energetic drive to meet goals with a strong hands-on, “can-do” approach&lt;br&gt;• Strives in moving in a fast-paced environment, including handling multiple calls/demos per day with immediate follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Cloud platforms like Azure &amp;amp;amp; AWS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift Timing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role requires working in the US time zone, with shift timings from 6:00 PM to 3:00 AM IST.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills And Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience with a SaaS company or demonstrable knowledge of SaaS practices&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of cloud-native IaaS &amp;amp;amp; PaaS services.&lt;br&gt;• A high level of business acumen and experience working with various cross-&lt;br&gt;functional stakeholders to foster collaboration in solving business challenges&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Fundamental knowledge of the NIST Cybersecurity 2.0 framework&lt;br&gt;Basic knowledge of cybersecurity solutions in the areas of EDR, XDR, MDR, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
